## SQ-ROLL-01 | Roll Delight member loads (ROLL-01)
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep -nE "roll_delight\|Roll Delight\|Error occurred while handling event" logs/latest.log \| head -30`; `grep -c "Error" logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass members line lists `roll_delight`; `Roll Delight upstream assets: N files`; no `Failed to parse` / loot table error naming `roll_delight`; no error in `roll_delight/*.js` (ROLL-01)
@fails donor missing or sha1 changed; generated loot JSON rejected (state range syntax)
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] members: \[.*\broll_delight\b
bootexpect Found new data pack roll_upstream_data
bootreject (?i)(failed to parse|loot table).*roll_delight
kjsreject (?i)(error|exception).*roll_delight/
shell echo "kubejs server.log Error lines: $(grep -c Error logs/kubejs/server.log)"; true

## SQ-ROLL-02 | chopstick foods and nether roll meat tags
@group A
@commands `/kubejs hand`-style checks or `/dumptags`: `#creativeengineering:chopstick_foods` holds `roll_delight:rice_roll_slice`, `farmersdelight:salmon_slice`, `minecraft:pufferfish`, `minecraft:cooked_cod`; `#roll_delight:nether_roll_meat` holds porkchop, bacon, prepared flesh
@pass all present
@fails tag script not run / helper name
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb passed
> zq itemtag creativeengineering:chopstick_foods
> zq itemtag roll_delight:nether_roll_meat
expect itemtag creativeengineering:chopstick_foods \(\d+\): .*roll_delight:rice_roll_slice
expect itemtag creativeengineering:chopstick_foods \(\d+\): .*farmersdelight:salmon_slice
expect itemtag creativeengineering:chopstick_foods \(\d+\): .*minecraft:pufferfish
expect itemtag creativeengineering:chopstick_foods \(\d+\): .*minecraft:cooked_cod
expect itemtag roll_delight:nether_roll_meat \(\d+\): .*minecraft:porkchop
expect itemtag roll_delight:nether_roll_meat \(\d+\): .*bacon
expect itemtag roll_delight:nether_roll_meat \(\d+\): .*prepared_flesh

## SQ-ROLL-03 | chopsticks lengthen the off-hand food's effects 1.5x (Glowing Calamari Roll; bot at 150)
@group A
@commands Bot: hunger 19 (`/effect give @p minecraft:hunger 2 255` then wait), main hand `roll_delight:chopsticks`, off hand `farmersdelight:cooked_rice`, use until eaten; `/data get entity @p foodLevel`; `/data get entity @p ActiveEffects`; `/data get entity @p SelectedItem`
@pass hunger 20 (capped), no Comfort (cooked rice has none; use a Comfort food to check the 1.5x duration), chopsticks Damage 1 (ROLL-07)
@fails Start/Finish hook: off-hand identity check, `getUsedItemHand`
@from batches/r1103/p2_R.qb
# r1103 p2: cooked rice has had no Comfort since the 2026-11-02 Comfort / Nourishment rules (comfort_nourishment.json
# "none"), so its read could not show the lengthening; hunger 19 -> 20 and chopsticks Damage 1 passed there
> zq food creativeengineering:glowing_calamari_roll
> pbot spawn rl3 150 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> clear rl3
> effect give rl3 minecraft:hunger 1 255
sleep 3
> data get entity rl3 foodLevel
> pbot hold rl3 roll_delight:chopsticks
> item replace entity rl3 weapon.offhand with creativeengineering:glowing_calamari_roll
> zq useitem rl3
sleep 5
> data get entity rl3 foodLevel
> data get entity rl3 ActiveEffects
expect has the following entity data: \[\{.*Duration
> data get entity rl3 SelectedItem
> data get entity rl3 Inventory
expect useitem rl3 offhand (CONSUME|SUCCESS)
expect has the following entity data: \{.*id: "roll_delight:chopsticks".*Damage: 1\b
> pbot remove rl3
look each ActiveEffects Duration is 1.5x the roll's own (the zq food line above; less the 5 s already ticked); off-hand roll gone

